-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 65 and 65.1 -- NO ASSIGNMENT OF A BENEFIT, AND ASSIGNING A RETIREMENT
-- PENSION TO A SPOUSE OR COMMON-LAW PARTNER.
--
-- Section 65 makes a benefit unassignable, unchargeable and exempt from seizure, with two exceptions that let
-- the Minister deduct what a provincial or municipal authority, or the administrator of a disability income
-- program, paid out in the meantime. Section 65.1 is the one deliberate exception to subsection 65(1): the
-- Minister may approve the assignment of a portion of a contributor's retirement pension to a spouse or common-law
-- partner. It says when, what an agreement or court order can do about it, how much is assigned (a share of each
-- of the three portions, weighted by months of cohabitation over months of joint contributory period), when the
-- assignment starts, and what ends it.
--
-- Out of range, taken as plain inputs: the retirement pension portions of paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c), as
-- adjusted under section 45 (piece cp3); the contributory periods of section 49, 49.1 and 49.2 and the months
-- excluded under paragraphs 49(c) and (d) (piece cp3); an agreement under section 80 (piece cp5); the days on which
-- persons "commence to live separate and apart within the meaning of paragraphs 55.1(2)(a) and (b)" (piece cp3);
-- regs 46.1 (notices in writing) and 78.2 (period of cohabitation), piece cr2. Regulation 76.1 sets the terms
-- of the deduction in subsection 65(3) and is encoded here with its figures ($50, one year), cited by the
-- locator form `src:C.R.C.-c.-385:N`.

§ `Section 65 -- benefit not to be assigned`

§§ `Section 65(1) and (1.1)`

-- A transaction that purports to deal with a benefit. The five kinds the subsection names, and any other.
-- src:2117 | 65 (1) A benefit shall not be assigned, charged, attached, anticipated or given as security, and any transaction purporting to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give as security a benefit is void.
@ref Act s 65(1) (src:2117)
DECLARE `cp4 Transaction in a benefit` IS ONE OF
    `an assignment of a benefit`
    `a charge on a benefit`
    `an attachment of a benefit`
    `an anticipation of a benefit`
    `a giving of a benefit as security`
    `another transaction in a benefit`

-- src:2116 | Benefit not to be assigned, etc.
-- src:2117 | 65 (1) A benefit shall not be assigned, charged, attached, anticipated or given as security, and any transaction purporting to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give as security a benefit is void.
@ref Act s 65(1) (src:2117)
GIVEN transaction IS A `cp4 Transaction in a benefit`
      `the transaction is an assignment of a portion of a retirement pension that the Minister has approved under section 65.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65(1) — the transaction is void` transaction `the transaction is an assignment of a portion of a retirement pension that the Minister has approved under section 65.1` MEANS
    -- Section 65.1(1) operates "notwithstanding subsection 65(1)": an assignment the Minister approves is not void.
    CONSIDER transaction
    WHEN `another transaction in a benefit` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an assignment of a benefit` THEN NOT `the transaction is an assignment of a portion of a retirement pension that the Minister has approved under section 65.1`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:2118 | Benefit not subject to seizure or execution
-- src:2119 | (1.1) A benefit is exempt from seizure and execution, either at law or in equity.
@ref Act s 65(1.1) (src:2119)
GIVEN `the thing seized or executed against is a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(1.1) — the benefit is exempt from seizure and execution` `the thing seized or executed against is a benefit` MEANS
    -- NOTHING for anything that is not a benefit: the subsection says nothing about it.
    IF `the thing seized or executed against is a benefit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 65(2) and (3) -- deductions the Minister may make`

-- src:2120 | Exception
-- src:2121 | (2) Notwithstanding subsections (1) and (1.1), where any provincial authority or municipal authority in a province pays a person any advance or assistance or welfare payment for a month or any portion of a month that would not be paid if a benefit under this Act had been paid for that period and subsequently a benefit becomes payable or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act to that person for that period, the Minister may, in accordance with any terms and conditions that may be prescribed, deduct from that benefit and pay to the provincial authority or municipal authority, as the case may be, an amount not exceeding the amount of the advance or assistance or welfare payment paid.
@ref Act s 65(2) (src:2121)
GIVEN `a provincial authority or a municipal authority in a province paid the person an advance, assistance or welfare payment for a month or any portion of a month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that payment would not be paid if a benefit under this Act had been paid for that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit subsequently becomes payable, or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act, to the person for that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the advance or assistance or welfare payment paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the benefit payable for that period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 65(2) — the most the Minister may deduct from the benefit and pay to the provincial or municipal authority` `a provincial authority or a municipal authority in a province paid the person an advance, assistance or welfare payment for a month or any portion of a month` `that payment would not be paid if a benefit under this Act had been paid for that period` `a benefit subsequently becomes payable, or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act, to the person for that period` `the amount of the advance or assistance or welfare payment paid` `the benefit payable for that period` MEANS
    -- "an amount not exceeding the amount of the advance ... paid", deducted from that benefit, so no more than the
    -- benefit itself (NOTES.md, fork register). NOTHING: the Minister has no such power.
    IF   `a provincial authority or a municipal authority in a province paid the person an advance, assistance or welfare payment for a month or any portion of a month`
     AND `that payment would not be paid if a benefit under this Act had been paid for that period`
     AND `a benefit subsequently becomes payable, or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act, to the person for that period`
    THEN JUST (min `the amount of the advance or assistance or welfare payment paid` `the benefit payable for that period`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2122 | Exception
-- src:2123 | (3) Despite subsections (1) and (1.1), if an administrator of a disability income program who is approved by the Minister makes a payment under that program to a person for a month or any portion of a month that would not have been made if a benefit under paragraph 44(1)(b) or (h) had been paid to that person for that period and subsequently a benefit becomes payable or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act to that person for that period, the Minister may, in accordance with any terms and conditions that may be prescribed, deduct from that benefit and pay to the administrator an amount not exceeding the amount of the payment made under that program.
@ref Act s 65(3) (src:2123)
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:767 | 76.1 (1) For the purposes of subsection 65(3) of the Act, the Minister may deduct an amount as described in that subsection from a benefit payable to a person under paragraph 44(1)(b) or (h) of the Act and pay that amount to an administrator approved by the Minister if
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:768 | (a) the administrator submits to the Minister a record of the payment made under the disability income program, together with the person’s irrevocable written consent to the deduction and payment;
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:769 | (b) the documents referred to in paragraph (a) are received by the Minister within one year after the date on which the consent is signed; and
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:770 | (c) the amount exceeds $50.
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:771 | (2) For the purpose of subsection 65(3) of the Act, if, for any reason, no deduction has been made or a deduction and payment have been made by the Minister for an amount that is less than the amount that might have been paid under that subsection, the Minister shall not authorize any other deduction and payment.
@ref Reg 76.1 (src:C.R.C.-c.-385:768-770)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of benefit`
      `the administrator of a disability income program is approved by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the administrator made a payment under that program for a month or any portion of a month that would not have been made if a benefit under paragraph 44(1)(b) or (h) had been paid to the person for that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit subsequently becomes payable, or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act, to the person for that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the administrator submitted a record of the payment together with the person's irrevocable written consent to the deduction and payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those documents were received by the Minister within one year after the date on which the consent was signed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the payment made under the program` IS A NUMBER
      `the benefit payable for that period` IS A NUMBER
      `no other deduction and payment has already been authorized for that payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 65(3) — the most the Minister may deduct from the benefit and pay to the administrator of a disability income program` kind `the administrator of a disability income program is approved by the Minister` `the administrator made a payment under that program for a month or any portion of a month that would not have been made if a benefit under paragraph 44(1)(b) or (h) had been paid to the person for that period` `a benefit subsequently becomes payable, or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act, to the person for that period` `the administrator submitted a record of the payment together with the person's irrevocable written consent to the deduction and payment` `those documents were received by the Minister within one year after the date on which the consent was signed` `the amount of the payment made under the program` `the benefit payable for that period` `no other deduction and payment has already been authorized for that payment` MEANS
    -- The terms the Act leaves to regulations are those of regulation 76.1 (piece cr2): the record and consent from
    -- the administrator, received within one year of the consent, an amount of more than $50, and only one
    -- opportunity (reg 76.1(2)). The benefit must be one under paragraph 44(1)(b) or (h).
    IF   (CONSIDER kind
          WHEN `a disability pension` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `a post-retirement disability benefit` THEN TRUE
          OTHERWISE FALSE)
     AND `the administrator of a disability income program is approved by the Minister`
     AND `the administrator made a payment under that program for a month or any portion of a month that would not have been made if a benefit under paragraph 44(1)(b) or (h) had been paid to the person for that period`
     AND `a benefit subsequently becomes payable, or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act, to the person for that period`
     AND `the administrator submitted a record of the payment together with the person's irrevocable written consent to the deduction and payment`
     AND `those documents were received by the Minister within one year after the date on which the consent was signed`
     AND `the amount of the payment made under the program` GREATER THAN 50
     AND `no other deduction and payment has already been authorized for that payment`
    THEN JUST (min `the amount of the payment made under the program` `the benefit payable for that period`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 65.1 -- assignment of retirement pension to spouse or common-law partner`

§§ `Section 65.1(3) and (4) -- agreements and court orders`

-- src:2129 | Agreement binding on Minister
-- src:2130 | (4) Where
-- src:2131 | (a) a written agreement between persons subject to an assignment under this section entered into on or after June 4, 1986 contains a provision that expressly mentions this Act and indicates the intention of the persons that there be no assignment under this section,
-- src:2132 | (b) that provision of the agreement is expressly permitted under the provincial law that governs such agreements,
-- src:2133 | (c) the agreement was entered into before the day of the application for the assignment, and
-- src:2134 | (d) that provision of the agreement has not been invalidated by a court order,
-- src:2135 | that provision of the agreement is binding on the Minister and, consequently, the Minister shall not approve an assignment under this section.
@ref Act s 65.1(4) (src:2130-2135)
GIVEN `the day the written agreement was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the agreement contains a provision that expressly mentions this Act and indicates the intention of the persons that there be no assignment under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that provision is expressly permitted under the provincial law that governs such agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the application for the assignment` IS A DATE
      `that provision has been invalidated by a court order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65.1(4) — a provision of the agreement binds the Minister, who shall not approve an assignment` `the day the written agreement was entered into` `the agreement contains a provision that expressly mentions this Act and indicates the intention of the persons that there be no assignment under this section` `that provision is expressly permitted under the provincial law that governs such agreements` `the day of the application for the assignment` `that provision has been invalidated by a court order` MEANS
        (`the day the written agreement was entered into` AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 1986 6 4) AND `the agreement contains a provision that expressly mentions this Act and indicates the intention of the persons that there be no assignment under this section`)
    AND `that provision is expressly permitted under the provincial law that governs such agreements`
    AND `the day the written agreement was entered into` LESS THAN `the day of the application for the assignment`
    AND (NOT `that provision has been invalidated by a court order`)

-- src:2127 | Agreement or court order not binding on Minister
-- src:2128 | (3) Except as provided in subsection (4), where, on or after June 4, 1986, a written agreement between persons subject to an assignment under this section was entered into, or a court order was made, the provisions of that agreement or court order are not binding on the Minister for the purposes of an assignment under this section.
@ref Act s 65.1(3) (src:2128)
GIVEN `the day the written agreement was entered into or the court order was made` IS A DATE
      `subsection (4) applies to a provision of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65.1(3) — the provisions of the agreement or court order are not binding on the Minister` `the day the written agreement was entered into or the court order was made` `subsection (4) applies to a provision of the agreement` MEANS
    -- NOTHING for an agreement or order before 4 June 1986: the subsection does not speak of them.
    IF `the day the written agreement was entered into or the court order was made` AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 1986 6 4)
    THEN JUST (NOT `subsection (4) applies to a provision of the agreement`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 65.1(6) and (7) -- when an assignment is made, and of which pensions`

-- src:2138 | Double assignment
-- src:2139 | (6) Where
-- src:2140 | (a) a retirement pension is payable to both spouses or to both common-law partners under this Act, or
-- src:2141 | (b) a retirement pension is payable to one spouse or to one common-law partner under this Act and a retirement pension is payable to the other spouse or common-law partner under a provincial pension plan and an agreement under section 80 provides for an assignment in this circumstance,
-- src:2142 | the assignment shall be made in respect of both retirement pensions and, in the case described in paragraph (b), in accordance with the agreement.
@ref Act s 65.1(6) (src:2139-2142)
GIVEN `a retirement pension is payable to both spouses or to both common-law partners under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a retirement pension is payable to one under this Act and a retirement pension is payable to the other under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an agreement under section 80 provides for an assignment in this circumstance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65.1(6) — the circumstances of a double assignment exist` `a retirement pension is payable to both spouses or to both common-law partners under this Act` `a retirement pension is payable to one under this Act and a retirement pension is payable to the other under a provincial pension plan` `an agreement under section 80 provides for an assignment in this circumstance` MEANS
        `a retirement pension is payable to both spouses or to both common-law partners under this Act`
    OR (`a retirement pension is payable to one under this Act and a retirement pension is payable to the other under a provincial pension plan` AND `an agreement under section 80 provides for an assignment in this circumstance`)

-- src:2143 | Single assignment
-- src:2144 | (7) Where, in respect of spouses or common-law partners,
-- src:2145 | (a) one is a contributor under this Act and the other is not a contributor under either this Act or a provincial pension plan,
-- src:2146 | (b) a retirement pension is payable under this Act to the contributor, and
-- src:2147 | (c) the non-contributor has reached sixty years of age,
-- src:2148 | the assignment shall be made only in respect of the retirement pension of the contributor.
@ref Act s 65.1(7) (src:2144-2148)
GIVEN `one is a contributor under this Act and the other is not a contributor under either this Act or a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a retirement pension is payable under this Act to the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the non-contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the age is tested` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65.1(7) — the circumstances of a single assignment exist` `one is a contributor under this Act and the other is not a contributor under either this Act or a provincial pension plan` `a retirement pension is payable under this Act to the contributor` `the non-contributor's date of birth` `the day on which the age is tested` MEANS
    -- "the non-contributor has reached sixty years of age": reaching 60 goes through section 2(2).
        `one is a contributor under this Act and the other is not a contributor under either this Act or a provincial pension plan`
    AND `a retirement pension is payable under this Act to the contributor`
    AND `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the non-contributor's date of birth` 60 `the day on which the age is tested`

-- The pensions an assignment is made in respect of.
-- src:2142 | the assignment shall be made in respect of both retirement pensions and, in the case described in paragraph (b), in accordance with the agreement.
@ref Act s 65.1(6) (src:2142)
-- src:2148 | the assignment shall be made only in respect of the retirement pension of the contributor.
@ref Act s 65.1(7) (src:2148)
DECLARE `cp4 Pensions an assignment covers` IS ONE OF
    `both retirement pensions`
    `only the contributor's retirement pension`
    `no assignment, for neither set of circumstances exists`

-- src:2142 | the assignment shall be made in respect of both retirement pensions and, in the case described in paragraph (b), in accordance with the agreement.
@ref Act s 65.1(6), (7) (src:2142), (src:2148)
GIVEN `the circumstances of a double assignment exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances of a single assignment exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `cp4 Pensions an assignment covers`
`s 65.1(6) and (7) — the pensions the assignment is made in respect of` `the circumstances of a double assignment exist` `the circumstances of a single assignment exist` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the circumstances of a double assignment exist` THEN `both retirement pensions`
        IF `the circumstances of a single assignment exist` THEN `only the contributor's retirement pension`
        OTHERWISE `no assignment, for neither set of circumstances exists`

-- src:2124 | Assignment of retirement pension to spouse or common-law partner
-- src:2125 | 65.1 (1) Notwithstanding subsection 65(1) but subject to this section, the Minister may approve the assignment of a portion of a contributor’s retirement pension to the contributor’s spouse or common-law partner, on application in prescribed manner and form by the contributor or the spouse or common-law partner, if the circumstances described in either subsection (6) or (7) exist.
@ref Act s 65.1(1) (src:2125)
GIVEN `an application in the prescribed manner and form has been made by the contributor or by the spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances described in subsection (6) or (7) exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (4) applies: a provision of an agreement binds the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65.1(1) — the Minister may approve the assignment` `an application in the prescribed manner and form has been made by the contributor or by the spouse or common-law partner` `the circumstances described in subsection (6) or (7) exist` `subsection (4) applies: a provision of an agreement binds the Minister` MEANS
    -- "the Minister may approve": the approval itself is the Minister's decision; these are the conditions. Subsection
    -- (4) ends with "the Minister shall not approve an assignment".
        `an application in the prescribed manner and form has been made by the contributor or by the spouse or common-law partner`
    AND `the circumstances described in subsection (6) or (7) exist`
    AND (NOT `subsection (4) applies: a provision of an agreement binds the Minister`)

-- src:2136 | Minister to notify parties
-- src:2137 | (5) The Minister shall, forthwith after receiving an application from one spouse or from one common-law partner for an assignment under this section, notify the other spouse or common-law partner, in prescribed manner, that such an application has been made, and of such other information as the Minister deems necessary.
@ref Act s 65.1(5) (src:2137)
GIVEN `the Minister has received an application from one spouse or one common-law partner for an assignment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65.1(5) — the Minister must at once notify the other spouse or common-law partner` `the Minister has received an application from one spouse or one common-law partner for an assignment` MEANS
    -- By notice in writing (reg 46.1(1), piece cr2).
    `the Minister has received an application from one spouse or one common-law partner for an assignment`

§§ `Section 65.1(8) -- definitions`

-- Not a provision: the number of months in a joint contributory period, the common shape of the three definitions
-- "joint contributory period", "first additional joint contributory period" and "second additional joint
-- contributory period": from the later of a fixed day and the month in which the elder reaches 18, to an end that
-- depends on whether both are contributors. The first and the last month are both counted.
GIVEN start IS A DATE
      `date of birth of one` IS A DATE
      `date of birth of the other` IS A DATE
      `both spouses or both common-law partners are contributors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the later of their respective contributory periods ends` IS A DATE
      `the month in which the contributor's contributory period ends` IS A DATE
      `the non-contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved` IS A DATE
      `the months excluded from the contributory periods of both` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp4 the number of months in a joint contributory period` start `date of birth of one` `date of birth of the other` `both spouses or both common-law partners are contributors` `the month in which the later of their respective contributory periods ends` `the month in which the contributor's contributory period ends` `the non-contributor's date of birth` `the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved` `the months excluded from the contributory periods of both` MEANS
    max 0 ((`the number of months from the month of one date to the month of another` `the start of the period` `the end of the period` PLUS 1) MINUS `the months excluded from the contributory periods of both`)
    WHERE
        -- "commencing on [the fixed day] or with the month in which the elder of the two ... reaches 18 years of age,
        -- whichever is later"; reaching 18 goes through section 2(2).
        `the elder's date of birth` MEANS
            IF `date of birth of one` AT MOST `date of birth of the other` THEN `date of birth of one` ELSE `date of birth of the other`
        `the month in which the elder reaches 18` MEANS `the month of a date` (`s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `any other provision` `the elder's date of birth` 18)
        `the start of the period` MEANS `cp4 the later of two months` start `the month in which the elder reaches 18`
        -- (a) both contributors: the month in which the later of their periods ends. (b) one contributor: the later of
        -- (i) the month the contributor's period ends and (ii) the earlier of the month the non-contributor reaches 70 and
        -- the month the application is approved.
        `the month in which the non-contributor reaches 70` MEANS `the month of a date` (`s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `any other provision` `the non-contributor's date of birth` 70)
        `the earlier of the month of 70 and the month of approval` MEANS
            IF `the month in which the non-contributor reaches 70` AT MOST `the month of a date` `the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved`
            THEN `the month in which the non-contributor reaches 70`
            ELSE `the month of a date` `the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved`
        `the end of the period` MEANS
            IF `both spouses or both common-law partners are contributors`
            THEN `the month of a date` `the month in which the later of their respective contributory periods ends`
            ELSE `cp4 the later of two months` `the month in which the contributor's contributory period ends` `the earlier of the month of 70 and the month of approval`

-- src:2156 | joint contributory period means the period commencing on January 1, 1966 or with the month in which the elder of the two spouses or of the two common-law partners reaches eighteen years of age, whichever is later, and ending
-- src:2157 | (a) where both spouses or common-law partners are contributors, with the month in which the later of their respective contributory periods ends, or
-- src:2158 | (b) where only one spouse or common-law partner is a contributor, with the later of
-- src:2159 | (i) the month in which the contributor’s contributory period ends, and
-- src:2160 | (ii) the earlier of the month in which the non-contributor reaches seventy years of age and the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved,
-- src:2161 | but excluding, where subsection (6) applies, any month that is excluded from the contributory period of both spouses or common-law partners pursuant to paragraph 49(c) or (d); (période cotisable conjointe)
@ref Act s 65.1(8) "joint contributory period" (src:2156-2161)
GIVEN `date of birth of one` IS A DATE
      `date of birth of the other` IS A DATE
      `both spouses or both common-law partners are contributors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the later of their respective contributory periods ends` IS A DATE
      `the month in which the contributor's contributory period ends` IS A DATE
      `the non-contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved` IS A DATE
      `subsection (6) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months excluded from the contributory period of both spouses or both common-law partners pursuant to paragraph 49(c) or (d)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 65.1(8) — the number of months in the joint contributory period` `date of birth of one` `date of birth of the other` `both spouses or both common-law partners are contributors` `the month in which the later of their respective contributory periods ends` `the month in which the contributor's contributory period ends` `the non-contributor's date of birth` `the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved` `subsection (6) applies` `the months excluded from the contributory period of both spouses or both common-law partners pursuant to paragraph 49(c) or (d)` MEANS
    -- "but excluding, where subsection (6) applies, any month that is excluded from the contributory period of both".
    `cp4 the number of months in a joint contributory period` (YearMonthDay 1966 1 1) `date of birth of one` `date of birth of the other` `both spouses or both common-law partners are contributors` `the month in which the later of their respective contributory periods ends` `the month in which the contributor's contributory period ends` `the non-contributor's date of birth` `the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved` (IF `subsection (6) applies` THEN `the months excluded from the contributory period of both spouses or both common-law partners pursuant to paragraph 49(c) or (d)` ELSE 0)

-- src:2149 | Definitions
-- src:2150 | (8) In subsection (9),
-- src:2151 | first additional joint contributory period means the period commencing on January 1, 2019 or with the month in which the elder of the two spouses or of the two common-law partners reaches 18 years of age, whichever is later, and ending
-- src:2152 | (a) if both spouses or common-law partners are contributors, with the month in which the later of their respective first additional contributory periods ends; or
-- src:2153 | (b) if only one spouse or common-law partner is a contributor, with the later of
-- src:2154 | (i) the month in which the contributor’s first additional contributory period ends, and
-- src:2155 | (ii) the earlier of the month in which the non-contributor reaches 70 years of age and the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved; (première période cotisable conjointe supplémentaire)
@ref Act s 65.1(8) "first additional joint contributory period" (src:2151-2155)
GIVEN `date of birth of one` IS A DATE
      `date of birth of the other` IS A DATE
      `both spouses or both common-law partners are contributors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the later of their respective first additional contributory periods ends` IS A DATE
      `the month in which the contributor's first additional contributory period ends` IS A DATE
      `the non-contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 65.1(8) — the number of months in the first additional joint contributory period` `date of birth of one` `date of birth of the other` `both spouses or both common-law partners are contributors` `the month in which the later of their respective first additional contributory periods ends` `the month in which the contributor's first additional contributory period ends` `the non-contributor's date of birth` `the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved` MEANS
    `cp4 the number of months in a joint contributory period` (YearMonthDay 2019 1 1) `date of birth of one` `date of birth of the other` `both spouses or both common-law partners are contributors` `the month in which the later of their respective first additional contributory periods ends` `the month in which the contributor's first additional contributory period ends` `the non-contributor's date of birth` `the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved` 0

-- src:2163 | second additional joint contributory period means the period commencing on January 1, 2024 or with the month in which the elder of the two spouses or of the two common-law partners reaches 18 years of age, whichever is later, and ending
-- src:2164 | (a) if both spouses or common-law partners are contributors, with the month in which the later of their respective second additional contributory periods ends; or
-- src:2165 | (b) if only one spouse or common-law partner is a contributor, with the later of
-- src:2166 | (i) the month in which the contributor’s second additional contributory period ends, and
-- src:2167 | (ii) the earlier of the month in which the non-contributor reaches 70 years of age and the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved. (deuxième période cotisable conjointe supplémentaire)
@ref Act s 65.1(8) "second additional joint contributory period" (src:2163-2167)
GIVEN `date of birth of one` IS A DATE
      `date of birth of the other` IS A DATE
      `both spouses or both common-law partners are contributors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the later of their respective second additional contributory periods ends` IS A DATE
      `the month in which the contributor's second additional contributory period ends` IS A DATE
      `the non-contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 65.1(8) — the number of months in the second additional joint contributory period` `date of birth of one` `date of birth of the other` `both spouses or both common-law partners are contributors` `the month in which the later of their respective second additional contributory periods ends` `the month in which the contributor's second additional contributory period ends` `the non-contributor's date of birth` `the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved` MEANS
    `cp4 the number of months in a joint contributory period` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) `date of birth of one` `date of birth of the other` `both spouses or both common-law partners are contributors` `the month in which the later of their respective second additional contributory periods ends` `the month in which the contributor's second additional contributory period ends` `the non-contributor's date of birth` `the month in which an application for an assignment of a retirement pension is approved` 0

-- src:2162 | period of cohabitation has the prescribed meaning, but in all cases shall be deemed to end with the month in which the joint contributory period ends; (période de cohabitation)
@ref Act s 65.1(8) "period of cohabitation" (src:2162)
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:799 | 78.2 For the purposes of subsection 65.1(8) of the Act, period of cohabitation means the period comprising all months during which the contributor and spouse or common-law partner referred to in subsection 65.1(9) of the Act cohabited, and includes the month in which their marriage was solemnized or in which they commenced to cohabit in a conjugal relationship, whichever is applicable, but does not include any months that are not within their joint contributory period as defined in subsection 65.1(8) of the Act.
@ref Reg 78.2 (src:C.R.C.-c.-385:799)
GIVEN `the month in which the marriage was solemnized or they commenced to cohabit in a conjugal relationship` IS A DATE
      `the last month in which they cohabited` IS A DATE
      `the first month of the joint contributory period` IS A DATE
      `the last month of the joint contributory period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 65.1(8) — the number of months in the period of cohabitation` `the month in which the marriage was solemnized or they commenced to cohabit in a conjugal relationship` `the last month in which they cohabited` `the first month of the joint contributory period` `the last month of the joint contributory period` MEANS
    -- The prescribed meaning (reg 78.2, piece cr2): all the months they cohabited, the month of the marriage or of
    -- starting to cohabit included, but no month outside the joint contributory period; the Act adds that it ends
    -- with the month the joint contributory period ends. The cohabitation is taken as one continuous run
    -- (NOTES.md, fork register).
    max 0 ((`the number of months from the month of one date to the month of another` `the first counted month` `the last counted month` PLUS 1))
    WHERE
        `the first counted month` MEANS `cp4 the later of two months` `the month in which the marriage was solemnized or they commenced to cohabit in a conjugal relationship` `the first month of the joint contributory period`
        `the last counted month` MEANS
            IF `the month of a date` `the last month in which they cohabited` AT MOST `the month of a date` `the last month of the joint contributory period`
            THEN `the month of a date` `the last month in which they cohabited`
            ELSE `the month of a date` `the last month of the joint contributory period`

§§ `Section 65.1(9) -- portion of pension to be assigned`

-- Not a provision: one term of subsection (9): the portion times 50% of the ratio of the months of cohabitation to
-- the months of the joint contributory period of its kind. NOTHING where the ratio has no denominator, unless the
-- portion is nil, in which case the term is nil.
GIVEN portion IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the period of cohabitation` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the joint contributory period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`cp4 a term of the portion assigned` portion `the number of months in the period of cohabitation` `the number of months in the joint contributory period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF portion EQUALS 0 THEN JUST 0
        IF `the number of months in the joint contributory period` EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST (portion TIMES (50% TIMES (`the number of months in the period of cohabitation` DIVIDED BY `the number of months in the joint contributory period`)))

-- src:2168 | Portion of pension assignable
-- src:2169 | (9) The portion of a contributor’s retirement pension to be assigned to the contributor’s spouse or common-law partner under this section is an amount equal to the aggregate of
-- src:2170 | (a) an amount calculated by multiplying
-- src:2171 | (i) the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension calculated as provided in paragraph 46(1)(a) and adjusted in accordance with section 45, by
-- src:2172 | (ii) 50% of the ratio that the number of months in the period of cohabitation bears to the number of months in the joint contributory period,
-- src:2173 | (b) an amount calculated by multiplying
-- src:2174 | (i) the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension, calculated as provided in paragraph 46(1)(b) and adjusted in accordance with section 45, by
-- src:2175 | (ii) 50% of the ratio that the number of months in the period of cohabitation bears to the number of months in the first additional joint contributory period, and
-- src:2176 | (c) an amount calculated by multiplying
-- src:2177 | (i) the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension, calculated as provided in paragraph 46(1)(c) and adjusted in accordance with section 45, by
-- src:2178 | (ii) 50% of the ratio that the number of months in the period of cohabitation bears to the number of months in the second additional joint contributory period.
@ref Act s 65.1(9) (src:2169-2178)
GIVEN portions IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the number of months in the period of cohabitation` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the joint contributory period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the first additional joint contributory period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the second additional joint contributory period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 65.1(9) — the portion of the contributor's retirement pension to be assigned` portions `the number of months in the period of cohabitation` `the number of months in the joint contributory period` `the number of months in the first additional joint contributory period` `the number of months in the second additional joint contributory period` MEANS
    -- The portions are those of paragraphs 46(1)(a), (b) and (c), adjusted in accordance with section 45 (piece cp3).
    -- The same period of cohabitation is the numerator of all three terms, as the text has it (NOTES.md, finding).
    CONSIDER `cp4 a term of the portion assigned` (portions's `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`) `the number of months in the period of cohabitation` `the number of months in the joint contributory period`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST base THEN
        CONSIDER `cp4 a term of the portion assigned` (portions's `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`) `the number of months in the period of cohabitation` `the number of months in the first additional joint contributory period`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST firstAdditional THEN
            CONSIDER `cp4 a term of the portion assigned` (portions's `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`) `the number of months in the period of cohabitation` `the number of months in the second additional joint contributory period`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST secondAdditional THEN JUST (base PLUS firstAdditional PLUS secondAdditional)

§§ `Section 65.1(10), (11), (11.1), (11.2) and (12) -- when an assignment starts and stops, and notice`

-- src:2179 | When assignment commences
-- src:2180 | (10) An assignment under this section commences with the month following the month in which the application for the assignment is approved.
@ref Act s 65.1(10) (src:2180)
GIVEN `the month in which the application for the assignment is approved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 65.1(10) — the month with which the assignment commences` `the month in which the application for the assignment is approved` MEANS
    `the month following the month of a date` `the month in which the application for the assignment is approved`

-- Not a provision: the earlier of two months, either of which may be missing (an event that has not happened).
GIVEN first IS A MAYBE DATE
      second IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`cp4 the earlier of two months that may be missing` first second MEANS
    CONSIDER first
    WHEN NOTHING THEN second
    WHEN JUST a THEN
        CONSIDER second
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST a
        WHEN JUST b THEN
            IF a AT MOST b THEN JUST a ELSE JUST b

-- src:2181 | When assignment ceases
-- src:2182 | (11) An assignment under this section ceases with the earliest of
-- src:2183 | (a) the month in which either spouse or either common-law partner dies,
-- src:2184 | (b) the twelfth month following the month in which the spouses or the common-law partners commence to live separate and apart within the meaning of paragraphs 55.1(2)(a) and (b) (and in those paragraphs a reference to “persons subject to a division” shall be read as a reference to “spouses or common-law partners”),
-- src:2185 | (c) where subsection (7) applies, the month in which the non-contributor spouse or the non-contributor common-law partner becomes a contributor,
-- src:2186 | (d) the month in which a decree absolute of divorce, a judgment granting a divorce under the Divorce Act or a judgment of nullity of a marriage is issued, and
-- src:2187 | (e) the month following the month in which the Minister approves a request or requests in writing from both spouses or both common-law partners that the assignment be cancelled.
@ref Act s 65.1(11) (src:2182-2187)
GIVEN `the day on which either spouse or either common-law partner dies` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the spouses or common-law partners commence to live separate and apart within the meaning of paragraphs 55.1(2)(a) and (b)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `subsection (7) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the non-contributor spouse or non-contributor common-law partner becomes a contributor` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which a decree absolute of divorce, a judgment granting a divorce under the Divorce Act or a judgment of nullity of a marriage is issued` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the Minister approves a request or requests in writing from both spouses or both common-law partners that the assignment be cancelled` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 65.1(11) — the month with which the assignment ceases` `the day on which either spouse or either common-law partner dies` `the day on which the spouses or common-law partners commence to live separate and apart within the meaning of paragraphs 55.1(2)(a) and (b)` `subsection (7) applies` `the day on which the non-contributor spouse or non-contributor common-law partner becomes a contributor` `the day on which a decree absolute of divorce, a judgment granting a divorce under the Divorce Act or a judgment of nullity of a marriage is issued` `the day on which the Minister approves a request or requests in writing from both spouses or both common-law partners that the assignment be cancelled` MEANS
    -- "ceases with the earliest of" the months below; NOTHING when none of these events has happened (the text
    -- then gives no end). Each event that has happened is turned into the month it names.
    `cp4 the earlier of two months that may be missing` `the month of death`
        (`cp4 the earlier of two months that may be missing` `the twelfth month following separation`
            (`cp4 the earlier of two months that may be missing` `the month of becoming a contributor`
                (`cp4 the earlier of two months that may be missing` `the month of the divorce or nullity` `the month following the approval of the request`)))
    WHERE
        `the month of death` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which either spouse or either common-law partner dies`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST day THEN JUST (`the month of a date` day)
        `the twelfth month following separation` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which the spouses or common-law partners commence to live separate and apart within the meaning of paragraphs 55.1(2)(a) and (b)`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST day THEN JUST (`add months` (`the month of a date` day) 12)
        -- (c) is an event only "where subsection (7) applies".
        `the month of becoming a contributor` MEANS
            IF `subsection (7) applies`
            THEN
                CONSIDER `the day on which the non-contributor spouse or non-contributor common-law partner becomes a contributor`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST day THEN JUST (`the month of a date` day)
            ELSE NOTHING
        `the month of the divorce or nullity` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which a decree absolute of divorce, a judgment granting a divorce under the Divorce Act or a judgment of nullity of a marriage is issued`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST day THEN JUST (`the month of a date` day)
        `the month following the approval of the request` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which the Minister approves a request or requests in writing from both spouses or both common-law partners that the assignment be cancelled`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST day THEN JUST (`the month following the month of a date` day)

-- src:2188 | Request for reinstatement
-- src:2189 | (11.1) Where paragraph (11)(e) applies, either spouse or either common-law partner may make a request in writing to the Minister to have the assignment reinstated.
@ref Act s 65.1(11.1) (src:2189)
GIVEN `the assignment ceased under paragraph (11)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65.1(11.1) — either spouse or either common-law partner may request in writing that the assignment be reinstated` `the assignment ceased under paragraph (11)(e)` MEANS
    `the assignment ceased under paragraph (11)(e)`

-- src:2190 | When reinstatement effective
-- src:2191 | (11.2) An assignment shall be reinstated on the first day of the month following the month in which the Minister approves the request referred to in subsection (11.1).
@ref Act s 65.1(11.2) (src:2191)
GIVEN `the day on which the Minister approves the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 65.1(11.2) — the day the assignment is reinstated` `the day on which the Minister approves the request` MEANS
    -- "on the first day of the month following the month in which the Minister approves the request"
    `the month following the month of a date` `the day on which the Minister approves the request`

-- src:2192 | Notification of assignment
-- src:2193 | (12) On approval by the Minister of an assignment under this section, both spouses or both common-law partners shall be notified in the prescribed manner.
@ref Act s 65.1(12) (src:2193)
GIVEN `the Minister has approved an assignment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65.1(12) — both spouses or both common-law partners must be notified` `the Minister has approved an assignment` MEANS
    -- By notice in writing with the month the assignment commences, the portion assigned and a statement of the right
    -- to request reconsideration (reg 46.1(2), piece cr2).
    `the Minister has approved an assignment`
